.TH MISSILE-DEFENSE 6 "2026-07-24" "missile-defense 0.1.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
missile\-defense \- faithful Atari Missile Command clone
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B missile\-defense
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Missile Defense
is a modern, faithful clone of Atari's Missile Command (1980), built on a
deterministic C++ simulation and rendered with Qt 6 and Vulkan. Defend six
cities from descending waves of ICBMs, splitting MIRVs and blast\-dodging smart
bombs by launching interceptors from three ammo\-limited batteries.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-play
Start a game immediately, skipping the menu.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Mouse
Move the crosshair to aim.
.TP
.B Left click
Fire from the nearest battery that has ammo.
.TP
.B Arrow keys / W, S + Enter
Navigate the menu (the mouse works too).
.TP
.B Esc / P
Pause to the menu.
.TP
.B F, M, A
Toggle fullscreen, music, and audio (sound effects).
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Jens Köhler, developed with Claude Code (Anthropic).
.SH HOMEPAGE
https://github.com/JensKSP/missile-defense
